# Environment for the Go live-feed gateway (services/realtime). Read in
# internal/config/config.go and cmd/realtime/main.go. Unset or empty means the default in the
# comment above each variable. Durations use Go syntax (30s, 4m). A bad value stops the process
# at start-up with exit code 2 rather than falling back silently.
#
# Secrets stay empty here. In Cloud Run they come from Secret Manager, in local compose from your
# shell or an untracked .env file. Never write a secret into this file.

# --- Server ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TCP port the HTTP server listens on, and the port the compose healthcheck probes. Optional, not
# secret. Default 8080 (compose publishes it on the host as REALTIME_HOST_PORT, default 8090).
PORT=8080

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres URL for the gateway's own read-only login, clinic_realtime (column-level SELECT on the
# event log). Required, secret. Locally `make up` creates the role and docker-compose.yml wires
# the URL for the realtime service; Cloud Run reads it from the Secret Manager secret
# clinic-database-url-realtime (direct Neon endpoint).
DATABASE_URL=
# Connections held per instance, 1 or 2 (anything else is rejected). Optional, not secret.
# Default 2.
DB_MAX_CONNS=2

# --- Auth ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key that verifies the signed staff assertion. Must equal the API's and the admin app's
# INTERNAL_SIGNING_KEY. Required, secret, at least 32 bytes. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# (the same value goes to all three). Cloud Run: Secret Manager clinic-internal-signing-key.
INTERNAL_SIGNING_KEY=
# Lets the release smoke open a stream as the synthetic "smoke" identity, which sees only the
# smoke's own events. Optional, secret; if set it must be at least 32 bytes, leave empty to turn
# the smoke identity off. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32. Cloud Run: Secret Manager
# clinic-smoke-signing-key.
SMOKE_SIGNING_KEY=
# Comma-separated owner emails; these people hold the owner role by configuration. Same value the
# API and the admin app read. Optional for the process to start, not secret. No default (empty
# means nobody is an owner by configuration). Locally set it to the address you sign in with.
ADMIN_EMAILS=

# --- Stream limits (cost guards) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Streams one instance serves at once; must be >= 1. Optional, not secret. Default 1.
MAX_STREAMS_PER_INSTANCE=1
# Streams one person may hold at once; must be >= 1. Optional, not secret. Default 1.
MAX_STREAMS_PER_PERSON=1
# Hard server-side ceiling on one stream; a ticket can only shorten it. Optional, not secret.
# Default 290s.
MAX_CONNECTION=290s
# Closes a stream that has delivered no appointment event for this long (heartbeats do not
# count). Optional, not secret. Default 240s.
IDLE_TIMEOUT=240s

# --- Timers ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How often the gateway polls the event log for new rows. Optional, not secret. Default 1s.
POLL_INTERVAL=1s
# Interval between heartbeat comments on an open stream. Start-up refuses anything under 25s
# (cost guard). Optional, not secret. Default 30s.
HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL=30s
# How often an open stream re-reads the person's role, so a revoke ends it within this time.
# Optional, not secret. Default 30s (docker-compose.yml sets 2s so the e2e can test a revoke).
ROLE_RECHECK=30s
# Time allowed to drain open streams on shutdown (Cloud Run allows 10s after SIGTERM). Optional,
# not secret. Default 8s.
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=8s

# --- Problem responses -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL for the "type" links in problem+json errors. Optional, not secret. Default
# https://clinic.invalid (a reserved TLD, so links go nowhere unless you set a real site).
PROBLEMS_BASE_URL=https://clinic.invalid

# --- Tests only (internal/testenv, cmd/realtime/main_test.go; services/realtime/Makefile sets them) ---
# The integration tests need `make up` from the repository root (database and API running).
# The Makefile fills the two DSNs and TEST_API_URL with ?=, which does not override a variable that
# is set but empty, and setting TEST_API_URL pins it. So those three are listed commented out.
# Owner-role connection string of the compose database, used to seed test data. Secret (a local
# throwaway); the Makefile sets it for `make test`, so only set it to run `go test` by hand.
# TEST_OWNER_DSN=
# Connection string for the clinic_realtime login of the same database. Secret (local throwaway);
# the Makefile sets it as well.
# TEST_REALTIME_DSN=
# Base URL of the running API the tests call. Not secret. Default (Makefile, `?=`)
# http://127.0.0.1:$(API_HOST_PORT), i.e. 8080 and following API_HOST_PORT. Commented out: setting
# it, even to 8080, pins it and it stops following API_HOST_PORT.
# TEST_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Must equal INTERNAL_SIGNING_KEY of that running API; the tests sign staff assertions with it
# and fail if it is empty. Secret, at least 32 bytes; use the same value you started the API with.
TEST_API_SIGNING_KEY=
